    {
      "name": "❌ Failing Endpoints — Corenio bug, needs escalation",
      "description": "All three fail identically with {\"error\":\"auth required!\"} HTTP 401 — a completely different error shape than Corenio's own structured format ({format,success,error_message:{code,message,details}}) used by every passing endpoint above, including sibling Carts endpoints using the IDENTICAL headers. Verified NOT a credentials/header problem: tried every combination (API key alone, real user Bearer alone, the working triple-header combo, all mixed) against these 3 routes specifically — same failure every time. This looks like a gateway/route-level auth check misconfigured only for these three item-mutation routes. Net effect: it is currently impossible to add anything to a Corenio cart through any path, which blocks the entire new Carts-based checkout flow at its first real step.",
